## Learning Logs

<img 
  src="https://images.code.org/c18d3fe17e942a2403603f27bb9890b8-image-1773163147667.17.11 AM.png" 
  alt="" 
  style="width: 30%; border-radius: 10px; margin: 0px 0px 10px 10px; float: right;">



#### Each milestone includes a Learning Log that spans its two-lesson arc. In their Learning Logs, students reflect on new understandings about AI and draft sections of their Responsible AI Use Guide, gradually building toward their final project.

### **Implementation Tips**

* #### **Set the Purpose Early**: Introduce the Learning Log as a working document, not a worksheet. Help students understand that this is where they will track evolving ideas, and draft their final project.

* #### **Model Thoughtful Reflection**: Show an example of a strong Learning Log entry. Demonstrate how to move beyond surface-level responses (“AI can be wrong”) to evidence-based reflection (“AI sounded confident but lacked source evidence, which made it less credible.”).

* #### **Use Logs as Formative Assessment**: Skim logs periodically to gauge understanding, misconceptions, and depth of reasoning.

